{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_020dbbbe40e23935016a9bc06745b487d19f9665fe4b10c122","text":"1. Apple: A crisp, sweet fruit with many varieties and colors.\n\n2. Banana: A soft, creamy tropical fruit wrapped in an easy-to-peel yellow skin.\n\n3. Orange: A juicy citrus fruit known for its bright flavor and vitamin C.\n\n4. Strawberry: A red, fragrant berry with tiny seeds on its outer surface.\n\n5. Mango: A rich, golden tropical fruit with sweet, aromatic flesh.\n\n6. Pineapple: A tangy, tropical fruit with a rough spiky rind and juicy interior.\n\n7. Grape: A small, round fruit that grows in clusters and may be sweet or tart.\n\n8. Watermelon: A large, refreshing melon with watery pink or red flesh.\n\n9. Peach: A fuzzy-skinned stone fruit with soft, sweet, fragrant flesh.\n\n10. Pear: A mild, juicy fruit with a distinctive rounded base and narrow top.\n\n11. Kiwi: A small brown fuzzy fruit with bright green flesh and edible black seeds.\n\n12. Cherry: A small, glossy stone fruit that is often sweet, tart, or both.\n\n13. Papaya: A tropical fruit with orange flesh and a center full of dark seeds.\n\n14. Pomegranate: A round fruit filled with jewel-like, tart-sweet red seeds.\n\n15. Blueberry: A small blue-purple berry with a sweet flavor and delicate skin.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null},"threadId":"01a07067-8116-7de0-85a2-33188daf6d1e","turnId":"01a07067-8181-7043-b2bf-630bf039622d","completedAtMs":1788592238744},"emittedAtMs":1788592238748}
